### libplctag native library (Mozilla Public License 2.0)

The `libplctag.NativeImport` package embeds the native libplctag C library
(`plctag.dll` / `libplctag.so`) as a resource of the .NET assembly of that
name. At run time lgx-mcp extracts it to a temporary directory and loads it
for CIP / EtherNet-IP access. The upstream project offers this library under
either the MPL-2.0 or the LGPL-2.0-or-later; lgx-mcp uses it under the
**MPL-2.0**. It is not modified by this project.

Source code for the native library, as MPL-2.0 section 3.2 requires, is
available from the upstream project at no charge:

- Source repository: <https://github.com/libplctag/libplctag>
- Releases and source archives: <https://github.com/libplctag/libplctag/releases>
- .NET wrapper and the packaging that embeds the binaries:
  <https://github.com/libplctag/libplctag.NET>

The embedded binaries are those that upstream built into
`libplctag.NativeImport` 1.0.0 (published September 2020). The full MPL-2.0
text is in [licenses/MPL-2.0.txt](licenses/MPL-2.0.txt). The MPL-2.0 covers
the libplctag files themselves; it does not apply to lgx-mcp's own source
code, which stays under the LICENSE file at the root of this repository.
